      "urpx:forRatePlan": {
        "@id": "gpc:et"
      },
      "urpx:hasCoverageClaim": {
        "@id": "gpc:cc-et-2026-06-01",
        "@type": "urpx:CoverageClaim",
        "urpx:completenessResult": {
          "@id": "urpx:partial"
        },
        "urpx:selfContained": true,
        "urpx:explainedBy": {
          "@type": "urpx:Evaluation",
          "@id": "gpc:cc-et-2026-06-01-evaluation",
          "urpx:evaluationKind": {
            "@id": "urpx:coverageEvaluation"
          },
          "urpx:description": "This filing does not carry everything its source document states. 5 parts are deferred, listed here in the same words as the filing's tariff.toml [modeling].deferrals so the two records cannot drift. (1) Fuel seasons by billing month, and period months. FCR-27 prices June through September and October through May, which Schedule R's bills show is read by the billing month a bill is rendered in. ET-23's period table names its months (JUNE-SEP, OCT-MAY) without saying whether they are calendar or billing months. The JSON-LD gates the fuel prices and the periods on calendar months, so usage in the weeks a billing period runs ahead of its billing month may take the other season's prices. (2) Voltage level and franchise fee location. ET-23 serves at 19,800 volts or higher, which FCR-27 classes as Primary Distribution or Transmission. Those two voltage levels and MFF-11's two locations are crossed in one ProfileAlternatives set of four alternatives, because URPX v0.5.1 allows one set per PlanElements and the franchise fee's energy subtotal must include that voltage level's fuel prices. A consumer selects one alternative, for example Primary Distribution inside city limits. (3) Municipal Franchise Fee base. MFF-11 applies to the total revenues of each bill, which include the ECCR-15 amount. Its multiplier Price here is based on the energy-and-fuel subtotal, not on the ECCR multiplier Price, so the franchise fee on that amount, about 0.40 percent of the base bill inside city limits, is not carried. (4) Hour after midnight at a season change. The hour after midnight takes the period of the day before, which the JSON-LD gates on the calendar month of that hour, so the first hour of October 1 and of June 1 takes the new season's after-midnight period, for example Period 6 at 5.2485 cents in the first hour of an October 1 that falls Tuesday through Saturday, where the sheet's Period 2 from September 30 is 5.6367 cents. (5) Term of Contract. Twenty years with automatic renewal for successive periods of five years. Nothing is priced by it and it is not carried.",
          "urpx:evaluatedOn": "2026-10-19T00:00:00"
        }
      }
    }
  }
